 (* agent note (|2026-09-15 STORAGE SUBSTRATE WATCH (operator review
      session, PP archaeology). Pricklypear's one-tree substrate
      autopsy, tl;dr: its "everything is a tree" storage bet froze at
      HALF-migrated (P3 read-flip done, P4 write-truth never retired
      the relational tables) and that intermediate dual-run state is
      precisely where weeks of vibecoding got spent: user-owned
      mutable path hierarchies force a path grammar, a label codec,
      branch-override walks, version shadows, sibling order, retention
      policies, and generations — seven subsystems, all paid for and
      none of them load-bearing for the calculus. LESSON, to be kept
      standing law for tuna1 AND tuna2: content-addressed VALUES are
      the primitive; mutable tree HIERARCHIES in PG storage are the
      vibecoding trap. tuna1's store (0001 flat tables) is clean; keep
      it so — every new table that prefers a path or a parent pointer
      over a hash should be questioned in review. Explored nightly
      drafts for v2 (D7: canonical-hash preimage off ternary text onto
      packed bitstream, plus post-GC temporal KV, Model-B
      merkelized-node materialization on demand) live outside this
